{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 81,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician upon Gittith, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "A Psalm",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Asaph. Sing aloud to God our strength: make a joyful noise to the God of Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take a psalm, and bring hither the timbrel, the pleasant harp with the psaltery.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blow the trumpet in the new moon, in the time appointed, on our solemn feast day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a statute for Israel, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a law of the God of Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This he ordained in Joseph ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a testimony, when he went out through the land of Egypt: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "where",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I heard a language ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I understood not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I removed his shoulder from the burden: his hands were delivered from the pots.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou calledst in trouble, and I delivered thee; I answered thee in the secret place of thunder: I proved thee at the waters of Meribah. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear, O my people, and I will testify to thee; O Israel, if thou wilt hearken to me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There shall no strange god be in thee; neither shalt thou worship any strange god.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD thy God who brought thee out of the land of Egypt: open thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But my people would not hearken to my voice; and Israel would not obey me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So I gave them up to their own hearts lust: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they walked in their own counsels.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O that my people had hearkened to me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Israel had walked in my ways!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I should soon have subdued their enemies, and turned my hand against their adversaries.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The haters of the LORD should have submitted themselves to him: and their time should have endured for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.81.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.81.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He would have fed them also with the finest of the wheat: and with honey out of the rock I should have satisfied thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
